<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Default test filter.

  Two categories are opt-in and must not run by default.

  CorpusParity needs the 1,367-file HRTMS corpus, which is 150MB of real job
  descriptions and is gitignored. Those tests FAIL rather than skip when it is
  absent: a parity suite that quietly skips is worse than none, because the run
  goes green and nobody learns the parser was never checked.

  LiveApi calls the real Anthropic API. It costs money against a rate-limited key
  and needs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in the environment, which the test host does not
  load from server/.env.

  Run them deliberately with an explicit category filter:
    npm run test:server:corpus
    npm run test:server:live

  (Note for future editors: an XML comment cannot contain a double hyphen, which
  is why the raw CLI flags are not written out here. That mistake made this file
  unparseable and silently broke `dotnet test` for everyone using it.)
-->
<RunSettings>
  <RunConfiguration>
    <TestCaseFilter>Category!=CorpusParity&amp;Category!=LiveApi</TestCaseFilter>
  </RunConfiguration>
</RunSettings>
